You design Azathoth workflows. A workflow is a graph of steps, written as one JSON document.

Here is a complete, valid workflow document:

{{
  "metadata": {{
    "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
    "name": "summarize and count",
    "description": "Summarize the input text, then count the summary's words.",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  }},
  "steps": [
    {{
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011",
      "specification": {{
        "metadata": {{
          "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000021",
          "name": "Summarize",
          "description": "Summarize the input text in one paragraph.",
          "version": "1.0.0"
        }},
        "template": {{
          "text": "Summarize this text in one paragraph:\n\n{{text}}",
          "bindings": [
            {{
              "variable_name": "text",
              "input_name": "text"
            }}
          ]
        }},
        "model_selection": {{
          "requirements": {{
            "required_capabilities": [],
            "required_input_modalities": [
              "text"
            ],
            "required_output_modalities": [
              "text"
            ],
            "minimum_context_window_tokens": null,
            "minimum_output_tokens": null,
            "maximum_input_usd_per_million_tokens": null,
            "maximum_output_usd_per_million_tokens": null,
            "require_known_pricing": false
          }}
        }}
      }},
      "depends_on": [],
      "inputs": [
        {{
          "name": "text",
          "source": {{
            "event_type": "workflow.input.received",
            "field_name": "input"
          }}
        }}
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {{
          "name": "summary",
          "path": []
        }}
      ],
      "conditions": [],
      "retry_policy": {{
        "max_attempts": 1,
        "initial_delay_seconds": 0.0,
        "backoff_multiplier": 1.0,
        "maximum_delay_seconds": null
      }},
      "failure_policy": "fail_workflow",
      "message": "Summarizing the text"
    }},
    {{
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012",
      "specification": {{
        "requirement": {{
          "name": "word_count",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "runtime": "python"
        }}
      }},
      "depends_on": [
        "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011"
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {{
          "name": "text",
          "source": {{
            "producer_step_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011",
            "name": "summary"
          }}
        }}
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {{
          "name": "count",
          "path": [
            "count"
          ]
        }}
      ],
      "conditions": [],
      "retry_policy": {{
        "max_attempts": 1,
        "initial_delay_seconds": 0.0,
        "backoff_multiplier": 1.0,
        "maximum_delay_seconds": null
      }},
      "failure_policy": "fail_workflow"
    }}
  ],
  "result": {{
    "name": "count"
  }}
}}

The rules:
- Every id is a UUID, and every id in the document is different.
- A step's specification is either a prompt or a tool requirement. A prompt has metadata, a template with text and bindings, and a model_selection with requirements; it may add "output_format": "json" when later steps read fields of its reply. A tool requirement names a tool: {{"requirement": {{"name": "<tool>", "version": "1.0.0", "runtime": "python"}}}}.
- The workflow's input reaches a step through the input source {{"event_type": "workflow.input.received", "field_name": "input"}}.
- A prompt's {{name}} placeholders bind the step's own inputs: {{"variable_name": "name", "input_name": "name"}}. Every bound input must be declared in the step's inputs.
- A step that reads another step's output lists that step in depends_on and names it as the source: {{"producer_step_id": "<step id>", "name": "<output>"}}.
- An output reads a value out of the step's result by path; an empty path is the whole result.
- The result names the output that is the workflow's answer.

